\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\lang4105\f0\fs20 The Ecopath software version 6 is planned to be maintained, supported and extended for a many years to come by the Ecopath Research and Development Consortium. Older versions up to version 5 are no longer supported.
\par \pard The Ecopath software is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the \cf1\ul GNU General Public License version 2 as published by the Free Software Foundation\cf0\ulnone . EwE is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of ERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU General Public License for more details.
\par 
\par Ecopath cannot be guaranteed to be free of bugs. However, all known bugs have been removed or flagged. Please consult the \cf1\ul Ecopath development online resources\cf0\ulnone  for the current status of development and known issues. Should you encounter problems or have questions, please do not hesitate to consult the \cf1\ul user forums\cf0\ulnone  or \cf1\ul contact us by email\cf0\ulnone .
\par 
\par You are encouraged to \cf1\ul register as a user in the Ecopath website\cf0\ulnone  to participate in the Ecopath community. We also invite you to send brief descriptions of your ecosystem models to us. We look forward to fruitful interactions with you.
\par 
\par The Ecopath Research and Development Consortium is committed to help users with their modelling efforts via the \cf1\ul user support subscriptions programme\cf0\ulnone . If you need assistance with your ecosystem model, or you would like us to comment, please \cf1\ul contact us by email\cf0\ulnone . If possible, attach your data file(s) in a zip-file as this will facilitate examination of your model. Your data will never be used or distributed without your explicit consent.
\par }
